Key Outcome of Milestone 1
Milestone 1 established a clear problem definition, confirmed data quality, and showed that normalization and advanced modeling would be needed due to large differences between applications.

Milestone 2: Feature Engineering, Modeling, and Evaluation
Purpose of Milestone 2
The purpose of Milestone 2 is to build machine learning models, improve features, and evaluate performance. This milestone answers the question: How well can we detect anomalies using machine learning?
Feature Engineering
To improve detection quality, raw features were transformed into normalized and relative features.
Key engineered features:
•	app_z: z score per application
•	app_pct: percentage deviation from app baseline
•	rolling_mean_7d: 7 day rolling average
•	weekend_flag: indicates weekend behavior
Modeling Approaches
We tested multiple supervised and unsupervised models.
Models tested:
•	K Nearest Neighbors (KNN)
•	Logistic Regression
•	Decision Tree
•	Isolation Forest
Evaluation Metrics
Models were evaluated using precision, recall, and F1 score. F1 score was the main metric due to class imbalance.
Model Performance Table
Model	Precision	Recall	F1 Score
KNN (k=5)	0.995	0.993	0.994
Logistic Regression	0.994	0.992	0.993
Decision Tree	0.999	0.860	0.924
Isolation Forest	0.910	0.880	0.895
Key Findings
•	KNN with k=5 performed best overall
•	Logistic Regression performed almost as well and was easier to explain
•	Decision Trees showed signs of overfitting
•	Normalized per app features greatly improved results
